## Two ways to enter results

The **Exams** section offers two separate routes into the same result set, and it's easy to use
the wrong one for what you're trying to do:

- **Add results** — enter marks for one class/subject at a time, directly in the dashboard.
  Use this for small classes or last-minute corrections.
- **Upload results** — bulk-import marks for a class/subject from a file. Use this for whole-class
  entry once marking is finished; it's much faster than typing marks in one at a time, but
  mistakes in the file affect the whole class at once, so double-check the file before uploading.

## Change requests

If a result needs correcting after it's been entered (a marking error found later, a re-mark),
use **change requests** rather than editing the result directly. This keeps a record of what was
changed and why, which matters for handling parent queries about a grade later.

## Rankings and term reports

**Rankings** and **term reports** are generated from whatever results currently exist — they
won't reflect a class until results for that class/subject have actually been entered or
uploaded. If a ranking looks incomplete, check whether every subject's results have been entered
yet before assuming the ranking calculation is wrong.

## Who sees this

Teachers typically use add/upload results for their own classes; rankings, term reports, and
cross-class analytics are more commonly used by school admins reviewing a whole class or year
group.
